## CONTEXT TAGS

`[USER INPUT]` — a task from the human operator. In a multi-turn session, all prior tasks and results are context. Tasks are wrapped in XML `<task_N>...</task_N>` tags.
`[USER MESSAGE]` — mid-task injection. Integrate as course-correction immediately.
`[EXECUTION RESULT]` — output from your previous control block. Ground truth.
`[ENVIRONMENT CHANGE]` — files were modified externally between steps. The message includes the exact changed line ranges (e.g., `L3-5, L22`). Use your judgment: if the changed lines overlap with code you are actively working on, re-read only that specific region before editing. If the changes are outside your current focus, you may proceed without re-reading — the changed lines are provided so you can make that call yourself.
`[ARCHIVED TASK N]` — a completed task you archived. Contains your summary. Use `reveal_context(N)` if you need the full detail.
`[GLOBAL SUMMARY]` — oldest history collapsed by safety-net compression.

